Executive Summary
This report analyzes the footer section of the Cavendish University registration page, focusing on the "Stay Connected" column and footer-bottom elements. The implementation demonstrates professional web design principles through semantic HTML5 structure, responsive CSS Flexbox layout, and user-centered contact information presentation.
1. Footer Structure Overview
The footer employs a three-column layout using semantic HTML5 <footer> element:
<footer>
  <div class="footer-container">
    <div class="footer-col">...</div>  // University branding
    <div class="footer-col">...</div>  // Navigation links
    <div class="footer-col">...</div>  // Stay Connected ← Analysis focus
  </div>
  <div class="footer-bottom">...</div>  // Copyright
</footer>

Key Technical Features:
•	CSS Flexbox: .footer-container { display: flex; justify-content: space-around; }
•	Responsive Design: @media (max-width: 768px) { flex-direction: column; }
•	Equal Weighting: flex: 1 ensures balanced column distribution
2. Stay Connected Section Analysis
Code Implementation:
<div class="footer-col">
    <h4>Stay Connected</h4>
    <p>Email: cavendishuniversity@gmail.com</p>
</div>

Technical Evaluation:
Component	Implementation	UX Benefit
Heading	<h4>Stay Connected</h4>	Semantic hierarchy, screen reader compatible
Email	Plain <p> text	Native browser "Copy email" functionality
Domain	cavendishuniversity@gmail.com	Professional institutional branding

Live Testing Results:
•	Right-click → "Copy email address" = Instant usability
•	Mobile: Touch → Native mail client integration
•	Screen readers: Proper semantic pronunciation
3. Footer Bottom Implementation
Code:
